invariant: INV-14
file: cfg.h
catches: test/tx-record-builds.sh
reason: cfg.h admits a CH_TX_PT of 16385, one byte over the 2^14 plaintext
  RFC 9846 section 5.1 lets one record carry. rec_seal checks the
  ciphertext's 2^14 + 256 and passes it, so a build that sets the value
  sends records that a peer advertising no record_size_limit, or one above
  2^14 + 1, must refuse with record_overflow. Every receiver in this tree
  advertises at most 2^14 + 1, so no loop here sees the extra byte, and
  only the compile at the edge objects.

--- old
_Static_assert(CH_TX_PT >= 512 && CH_TX_PT <= 16384, "CH_TX_PT runs from 512 to 2^14");
--- new
_Static_assert(CH_TX_PT >= 512 && CH_TX_PT <= 16385, "CH_TX_PT runs from 512 to 2^14");
